cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Analysis code and database for "Non-cereal agroforestry as a globally
  overlooked reservoir of biodiversity and nutritional diversity"
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying database, please cite both the
  archived release and the associated article.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Beillouin
    given-names: Damien
    affiliation: CIRAD, UPR HortSys, Montpellier, France
    email: d.beillouin@cirad.fr
  - family-names: Jones
    given-names: Sarah K.
    affiliation: Bioversity International, Montpellier, France
abstract: >-
  R code and curated database used to produce all analyses and figures of a
  global systematic review of non-cereal agroforestry systems, covering 4,512
  paired experiments from 638 studies across 83 countries.
keywords:
  - agroforestry
  - agrobiodiversity
  - systematic review
  - threatened species
  - plant co-occurrence networks
  - ecosystem services
